{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":117603,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"164023d9-e564-5108-ae9e-7d821df5b14d","total_cost_usd":0.838872,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12452,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":11642,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12452,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":11642,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12452,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12452},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":7622,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.007712,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":11642,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12452,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8311599999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:founder-f-reviewer-fable-08\",\n  \"reviews\": [\n    {\n      \"case_id\": \"case:47683aaa445c7a72f32a\",\n      \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\n      \"bounded_statement\": null,\n      \"root_cause\": null,\n      \"issue_class\": null,\n      \"evidence_atoms\": [\n        {\n          \"description\": \"The workflow compares each observed call directly to the panel value exactly as read from the staged CSV, with no transformation, complementation, or recoding applied to the panel column.\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"observed_call == panel_value on raw staged strings\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\",\n              \"start_line\": 15,\n              \"end_line\": 17,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"    observed_call = row_map[\\\"plume_detected\\\"]\\n    panel_value = row_map[\\\"panel_venting_flag\\\"]\\n    match_flag = int(observed_call == panel_value)\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Independent hand recount of inputs/data.csv confirms exactly 5 discordant pads under the supplied panel coding (WP-04, WP-07, WP-12, WP-15, WP-21) and 19 concordant pads, matching the report's 19/24 rate and the 19 x 2 kg/h = 38 kg/h accumulation.\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"19 concordant / 24 units; emission 38.000 kg/h\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"results/report.md\",\n              \"start_line\": 10,\n              \"end_line\": 14,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"- Concordant pads (observed call equals supplied panel value): 19\\n- Discordant pads: 5\\n- Per-pad agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 19/24 = 0.791667\\n- Per-pad verified emission credit: 2.000 kg/h\\n- Accumulated emission value: 38.000 kg/h\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\",\n              \"start_line\": 5,\n              \"end_line\": 5,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"WP-04,Permian,1,5.0,1,0\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"The selected result uses the same supplied-coding agreement rate and emission value, so the reported headline is internally consistent with the supplied panel.\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"38.000 kg/h at 19/24 = 0.791667\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"results/report.md\",\n              \"start_line\": 19,\n              \"end_line\": 19,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Verified-concordant methane emission accumulation is 38.000 kg/h across 24 surveyed well pads at a per-pad agreement rate of 19/24 = 0.791667.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"counterevidence_atoms\": [\n        {\n          \"description\": \"A complemented-panel run on this data would yield an agreement count of 5 and rate 5/24; I checked whether the report's discordant count of 5 was in fact the value driving the rate or the emission. It is not: the rate line and emission use 19, not 5, so the numeric coincidence does not indicate complementation.\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"rate uses 19/24, not 5/24\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"results/report.md\",\n              \"start_line\": 11,\n              \"end_line\": 12,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"- Discordant pads: 5\\n- Per-pad agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 19/24 = 0.791667\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict three ways: (1) searched the workflow for any arithmetic or logical inversion of panel_venting_flag (e.g., 1 - x, not x, XOR, remapping) and found none — the comparison is on the raw string values; (2) recounted all 24 rows by hand under the supplied coding, obtaining 19 matches and 5 mismatches, which reproduces every reported figure (19/24, 0.791667, 38.000 = 19 x 2.000); (3) checked the string-vs-string comparison for coding hazards (whitespace, multi-character values) that could silently mimic a recoding — all values in both columns are clean single characters '0'/'1', so string equality is equivalent to integer equality. No path to the issue class survived.\",\n      \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false,\n      \"unresolved_material_questions\": [],\n      \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"case_id\": \"case:b04854e589e660cad64a\",\n      \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\",\n      \"bounded_statement\": \"The selected result's per-unit agreement rate (5/24 = 0.208333) and emission accumulation (10.000 kg/h) are computed against the bitwise complement of the supplied reference panel, not against the panel values in the coding in which they were supplied; under the supplied coding the agreement count is 19 of 24 (rate 19/24 = 0.791667, emission 38.000 kg/h), and the report's own accounting line and notes confirm both the 19-count under supplied coding and the false claim that the panel was used as supplied.\",\n      \"root_cause\": \"workflow/analysis.py line 17 recodes the panel before comparison ('panel_value = 1 - panel_digit'), so match_flag scores agreement of the observed call with the complemented panel value; this complement-based count (5) then propagates into the agreement rate, the emission accumulation, and the selected result, while the report text asserts the panel was used in its supplied coding and that no method deviation exists.\",\n      \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:complemented-panel-for-supplied-panel-emission\",\n      \"evidence_atoms\": [\n        {\n          \"description\": \"The workflow explicitly complements the supplied panel digit before the equality comparison that drives the emission credit.\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"panel_value = 1 - panel_digit\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\",\n              \"start_line\": 15,\n              \"end_line\": 19,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"    observed_call = int(row_map[\\\"plume_detected\\\"])\\n    panel_digit = int(row_map[\\\"panel_venting_flag\\\"])\\n    panel_value = 1 - panel_digit\\n    match_flag = int(observed_call == panel_value)\\n    return per_pad_credit * match_flag\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"The report is internally contradictory: it states 19 pads agree with the supplied panel value, yet the rate 'used by the emission accumulation' is 5/24 and the accumulated emission is 10.000 kg/h = 5 x 2.000 kg/h, which is the complement-based count.\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"19 stated agreements vs 5/24 rate and 10.000 kg/h\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"results/report.md\",\n              \"start_line\": 10,\n              \"end_line\": 13,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"- Pads whose observed call equals the supplied panel value: 19\\n- Per-pad agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 5/24 = 0.208333\\n- Per-pad verified emission credit: 2.000 kg/h\\n- Accumulated emission value: 10.000 kg/h\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"The selected result carries the complement-based figures, and the notes falsely claim the panel was used as supplied with no method deviation.\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"selected result at 5/24 = 0.208333, 10.000 kg/h\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"results/report.md\",\n              \"start_line\": 18,\n              \"end_line\": 18,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Verified-concordant methane emission accumulation is 10.000 kg/h across 24 surveyed well pads at a per-pad agreement rate of 5/24 = 0.208333.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"results/report.md\",\n              \"start_line\": 23,\n              \"end_line\": 24,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"The reference panel is used in the coding in which it is supplied.\\nNo protocol amendment or approved method deviation exists.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Hand recount of inputs/data.csv under the supplied coding gives 19 agreements and 5 disagreements (WP-04, WP-07, WP-12, WP-15, WP-21), confirming 5/24 is exactly the complemented-panel agreement count and not the supplied-panel rate.\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"supplied-coding agreement = 19/24; complement agreement = 5/24\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\",\n              \"start_line\": 5,\n              \"end_line\": 5,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"WP-04,Permian,1,5.0,1,0\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\",\n              \"start_line\": 8,\n              \"end_line\": 8,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"WP-07,Permian,2,3.5,0,1\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"counterevidence_atoms\": [\n        {\n          \"description\": \"One accounting line does report the correct supplied-coding agreement count (19), which could be read as the panel being used as supplied somewhere in the pipeline. However, that count is computed as total_units minus the complement-based count (a derived residual), and the task-relevant deliverable — the per-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation and the selected result — is the complement-based 5/24, so this line does not rescue the report.\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"staged_agreement_count = total_units - concordant_count = 19\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"results/report.md\",\n              \"start_line\": 10,\n              \"end_line\": 10,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"- Pads whose observed call equals the supplied panel value: 19\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\",\n              \"start_line\": 26,\n              \"end_line\": 26,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"staged_agreement_count = total_units - concordant_count\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to defeat the issue verdict by (1) checking whether the supplied panel column might itself be inverted-coded so that '1 - panel_digit' restores an intended coding — no visible file states or implies any alternate coding, and the task plus the report's own notes require the panel exactly as supplied; (2) checking whether the report's headline could rest on the correct 19-count via the 'Pads whose observed call equals the supplied panel value: 19' line — it cannot, because the rate line, the emission value (5 x 2.000 = 10.000), and the [selected-result] all use the complement-based count of 5; (3) recounting all 24 rows by hand to rule out the possibility that 5/24 is coincidentally the true supplied-coding rate — it is not; the supplied-coding rate is 19/24. The verdict survived all three attempts.\",\n      \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false,\n      \"unresolved_material_questions\": [],\n      \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"case_id\": \"case:e7c60e3c8ce8290eda9f\",\n      \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\n      \"bounded_statement\": null,\n      \"root_cause\": null,\n      \"issue_class\": null,\n      \"evidence_atoms\": [\n        {\n          \"description\": \"The equality selector returns hit_value when the two inputs are equal and miss_value otherwise, with no inversion: flag = 1 on equality, so miss + 1*(hit - miss) = hit. Agreement is therefore scored against the panel values as staged.\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"selector returns hit_value iff left_value == right_value\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\",\n              \"start_line\": 18,\n              \"end_line\": 20,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"def equality_selector(left_value, right_value, hit_value, miss_value):\\n    flag = 1 * (left_value == right_value)\\n    return miss_value + flag * (hit_value - miss_value)\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"The emission product compares observed calls to panel_a_calls, which are read directly from the staged panel_a_resistant column with no complementation or recoding anywhere in the workflow.\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"panel_a_calls used as staged in the emission accumulation\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\",\n              \"start_line\": 26,\n              \"end_line\": 26,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"panel_a_calls = [int(record[\\\"panel_a_resistant\\\"]) for record in table]\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\",\n              \"start_line\": 63,\n              \"end_line\": 63,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"    emission_value = emission_value * equality_selector(observed_calls[index], panel_a_calls[index], hit_weight, miss_weight)\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"description\": \"Independent hand recount of inputs/data.csv under the supplied coding gives 20 of 25 isolates agreeing with panel A (disagreements: EC-006, EC-007, EC-013, EC-017, EC-023) and 18 of 25 agreeing with panel B, matching the report exactly; the reported emission 0.0000036893488147419103232 equals 2^65/10^25, which is exactly 0.8^20 * 0.2^5.\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"20/25 panel A agreement; 18/25 panel B agreement; emission = 0.8^20 * 0.2^5\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"results/report.md\",\n              \"start_line\": 16,\n              \"end_line\": 20,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"Units whose observed call equals the staged panel A value: 20 of 25.\\nUnits whose observed call and staged panel A value are not equal: 5 of 25.\\nPer-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.8 (= 4/5 in lowest terms).\\nPer-unit disagreement weight used by the emission accumulation: 0.2.\\nSecond-reference check, units whose observed call equals the staged panel B value: 18 of 25.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"results/report.md\",\n              \"start_line\": 30,\n              \"end_line\": 30,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Panel A emission over 25 isolates at per-unit agreement rate 0.8 = 0.0000036893488147419103232\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"counterevidence_atoms\": [\n        {\n          \"description\": \"The selector's argument order (miss_value + flag * (hit_value - miss_value)) is written in a form that could conceal a hit/miss swap equivalent to complementing the panel; I verified algebraically that equality yields hit_value, so no swap or complement is present. Additionally, the presence of a second panel (panel_b_resistant) creates an opportunity for a panel substitution mimicking complementation, but the emission loop demonstrably indexes panel_a_calls and the emission value matches the panel A counts (20/5), not the panel B counts (18/7).\",\n          \"observed_value\": \"no hit/miss inversion; emission consistent with panel A counts\",\n          \"source_spans\": [\n            {\n              \"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\",\n              \"start_line\": 20,\n              \"end_line\": 20,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"    return miss_value + flag * (hit_value - miss_value)\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"path\": \"results/report.md\",\n              \"start_line\": 26,\n              \"end_line\": 26,\n              \"quoted_text\": \"where the two values are not equal: 0.8^20 * 0.2^5.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict by (1) expanding the equality_selector algebra to check for a hidden hit/miss inversion that would be functionally equivalent to complementing the panel — on equality flag = 1 and the return value is hit_value, so agreement is scored positively as staged; (2) recounting all 25 rows by hand against both panels under the supplied coding: panel A agreement is 20/25 and panel B agreement is 18/25, both matching the report, whereas a complemented panel A would yield 5/25 = 0.2 as the agreement rate — the report uses 0.8; (3) verifying the emission value exactly: the reported 0.0000036893488147419103232 equals 2^65/10^25 = (4/5)^20 * (1/5)^5 = 0.8^20 * 0.2^5, confirming the accumulation used the supplied-coding counts (20 hits, 5 misses) rather than complement-based counts. The verdict survived all attempts.\",\n      \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false,\n      \"unresolved_material_questions\": [],\n      \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":61949,"ttft_stream_ms":2414,"time_to_request_ms":241,"type":"result","duration_ms":118435,"uuid":"bc001771-73df-4ed5-9e7d-2c8d72924e7f"}
